==English==

===Etymology===
Borrowed from {{etyl|it}} {{term|ballerina|lang=it}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈbæl.ɜː(ɹ).in.ə(ɹ)/}}, {{SAMPA|/"b{l.3:(r).in.@(r)/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A female [[ballet]] [[dancer]].
# {{context|less common|sometimes|derogatory}} A male ballet dancer.

====Usage notes====
Although normally used to refer only to females, it can be used of males although this is sometimes done so derogatorily. ''[[danseur]]'' or ''[[ballet dancer]]'' is the normal term for men.

